# Project Standards

This file is the **normative source of truth** for project standards. If another guidance file (for example, `.cursor/background.json` or a skill) differs, follow this file.

## Formatting

- **indentSize**: 2
- **useTabs**: true
- **trimTrailingWhitespace**: true
- **insertFinalNewline**: true
- **trailingComma**: "all"
- **semi**: true (semicolons required)
- **singleQuote**: true (single quotes only)
- **maxLineLength**: 100 characters

## Quality Gates

- **enforceTypeScript**: preferred for new/modified modules when practical in this mixed JS/TS codebase
- **enforceESLint**: true
- **enforcePrettier**: true

## Search Exclude Patterns

- node_modules/**, dist/**, data/**, client/assets/video/**
- **/*.png, **/*.jpg, **/*.jpeg, **/*.gif, **/*.svg, **/*.ico, **/*.webp
- **/*.mp4, **/*.mp3, **/*.wav, **/*.ogg, **/*.flac
- **/.DS_Store, **/*.log, records.json, report.html

## Naming Conventions

| Type | Pattern | Example |
|------|---------|---------|
| **Function** | ^[a-z][a-zA-Z0-9]*$ | appleTree |
| **CSS Class** | ^[a-z][a-z0-9-]*$ | apple-tree |
| **Class Name** | ^[A-Z][a-zA-Z0-9]*$ | AppleTree |
| **Constant** | ^[A-Z][A-Z0-9_]*$ | APPLE_TREE |

## Coding style

**Default: simple over clever.** The most important rule: do not make code complex—especially for hotfixes, naming, and templates.

### Before every fix

Ask: **hotfix or root cause?**

| Choose root cause when | A hotfix is acceptable when |
|------------------------|-----------------------------|
| The bug will recur without fixing the real path | Cause is unknown and investigation is costly |
| One config, condition, or missing field explains it | Change is tiny, scoped, and reversible |
| You are adding layers (helpers, loops, rewriters) to mask a symptom | Production is blocked and you will follow up |

Prefer the **smallest change that fixes the real cause**, not the most general framework.

### Simplicity

- **One name, one source of truth** — e.g. a single `welcomeImage` in config reused by preload and EJS; avoid string-matching in templates.
- **Extract a function only when** the logic is genuinely common **and** used in **at least two places**. One call site → inline it; do not wrap.
- **Names match the domain** — avoid overloading `context`, `ctx`, and `exportObj` without checking what each layer already means.
- **Reuse existing utilities** (`getSrc`, `getHref`, config fields) instead of parallel logic in EJS or webpack.

### Preload (`meta.preload` / route `preload` hook)

- Each entry must use **`href` as an absolute URL with host** (e.g. `https://cdn.example.com/images/foo.webp`).
- **Do not** pass path-only values (`/images/foo.webp`) or rely on EJS/`html_above.ejs` to add the domain.
- Build the full URL once in config `get()` (e.g. `getImgCdnUrl(cdnHost, path)`), reuse the same string for preload and template `src`.

### Listing data pipeline

- Architecture and demo trace: **`docs/listing-data-pipeline.md`**.
- Controllers: after `mapPropertyDetailToArticle` (or list mappers), use **`detail.metadata`**, **`detail.*` comp fields**, and **`buildDetailSeo(detail)`** only — not raw SOA listing for SEO or EJS.

### SOA Pure listing data

- Treat **SOA Pure** fields as the source of truth after `mapSOADataToMetadata` (list cards: `mapPropertyToArticle`; detail page: `mapPropertyDetailToArticle`).
- **Do not** add `??` / `||` fallbacks to alternate field names, legacy shapes, or synthetic defaults unless the user explicitly asks.
- If a required SOA field is missing, return empty / omit the UI piece — do not substitute `propertyId`, `fullAddress`, or guessed aliases.

### Anti-patterns

- Template loops or regex to find data that should live on `data` or config.
- New pipelines (`basePath` rewriters, extra env flags) when webpack `publicPath` or env loading is wrong.
- Duplicating the same path or URL in two places without a shared constant.
- Preload entries with `path` and no host (templates read `href` only).
- Fallback chains on SOA-mapped metadata (e.g. `fullAddress || propertyId` for display text).

## Code Reuse

**Rule**: Maximum reuse of utilities code.

**Requirements**:
- Always check existing utilities before implementing new functionality
- Import and reuse utility functions from `client/js/core/` and `helpers/` directories
- Never duplicate utility functionality - use existing utilities instead
- If similar functionality exists, extend or refactor existing utilities rather than creating duplicates
- Before writing new helper functions, search for existing utilities that can be reused or extended

**Utility Locations**:
- `client/js/core/` - Core client-side utilities (format, validate, query, log, load, etc.)
- `helpers/` - Server-side and shared utilities (geo, fuse, mappers, etc.)

**Checklist**:
- Search existing utilities before implementing new functionality
- Import from appropriate utility modules
- Extend existing utilities if needed rather than duplicating
- Document any new utility functions added

## Operational Conventions

- Prefer `rg` and project tools for search; avoid `grep`/`find` in agent workflows
- Keep guidance and examples aligned with real repo paths and scripts
- When a rule changes behavior, update related skills and docs in the same pass

## Documentation alignment

When you change architecture, routes, build scripts, ports, or CMS/theme conventions, update the **canonical** docs in the same pass where practical:

- `README.md`, `client.md`, `server.md`, `build-system.md`
- `docs/listing-data-pipeline.md`, `docs/development-workflow.md`, `docs/routes-reference.md`
- `.cursor/background.json` (high-level context for agents)
- Theme/CMS API details: `cms/API.md` and `.cursor/rules/theme-change.mdc`

Normative standards stay in this file; narrative architecture stays in the markdown docs above.
